# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5 (the current Sonnet-tier model).
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Optional. Effort level for the generation call: low | medium | high | xhigh | max
# Higher = more thorough spec reading, more tokens, longer runtime. Default: high
# ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=high

# Optional. Path to a Chrome/Edge executable used for PDF rendering. If unset,
# the app auto-detects Chrome then Edge on Windows/macOS/Linux.
#
# On a self-hosted server this is a real setting, not just a development one:
# Ubuntu installs chromium as a snap at /snap/bin/chromium, which is NOT on the
# auto-detect list, so rendering fails on a machine that visibly has Chromium.
# Install Google Chrome proper, or point this at the actual binary.
# On Vercel this is ignored - @sparticuz/chromium is used instead.
# LOCAL_CHROME_PATH=C:\Program Files\Google\Chrome\Application\chrome.exe

# --- Access control ------------------------------------------------------------
# BCH runs this inside the network with no sign-in: reaching it at all requires
# being on the LAN or the VPN. That has to be stated deliberately — a deployment
# with neither this nor sign-in credentials refuses to serve, so that an
# unfinished setup cannot quietly end up open.
ACCESS_CONTROL=network-only

# --- Sign-in (Microsoft Entra ID) — not in use ---------------------------------
# If sign-in is ever wanted instead, remove ACCESS_CONTROL above and set these.
# Note the redirect URI must be https: Entra refuses plain http for anything but
# localhost, so the server would then need a certificate.
#
#   AUTH_MICROSOFT_ENTRA_ID_ID=
#   AUTH_MICROSOFT_ENTRA_ID_SECRET=
#   AUTH_MICROSOFT_ENTRA_ID_ISSUER=https://login.microsoftonline.com/<TENANT-ID>/v2.0
#   AUTH_SECRET=            # node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#   AUTH_URL=https://cheatsheets.bch.local
